# Protection from blue stops blue creatures blocking the enchanted creature (CR 702.16f) though Blue Ward's Aura
# stays. Bot2's Devoted Hero wears Blue Ward and attacks on turn 4: Bot1's blue Aegis Turtle may not block it (the
# refusal), while the black Cabal Evangel may (the positive control), so Bot1 takes no damage.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Cabal Evangel
Aegis Turtle
Swamp x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Devoted Hero
Blue Ward
Plains x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: B)
Bot1.Hand.Cabal Evangel.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Aegis Turtle.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Devoted Hero.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Blue Ward.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Devoted Hero)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Blue Ward.AttachedTo = Devoted Hero
? Bot2.Battlefield.Devoted Hero.ProtectionFrom = Blue
Bot2.Attack(Devoted Hero > Bot1)
! Bot1.Block(Aegis Turtle > Devoted Hero)
Bot1.Block(Cabal Evangel > Devoted Hero)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]
[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Cabal Evangel.Damage = 1
Bot2.Graveyard = Blue Ward; Devoted Hero
Bot1.Life = 20
